{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["<b>Blessed be YHWH, the Elohim of Shem.</b> We are obligated to add praise to Shem, that He is the Elohim of Shem, and that He will make Canaan a slave to him and to Shem. The meaning is that He will compel him to serve Shem, for the word למו is like להם, and the vav is added as in תביאמו (Exodus 15:17); therefore, with the absence of the heh and without the vav, it does not occur [elsewhere]. And He mentioned alongside Shem the Name, the honored and awesome One, for the honor of Shem, and the case of Japheth is not like it. The Gaon [Saadia] said that the word 'my father' is missing, and it should have read 'cursed be my father Canaan.' He said it is like לעיני חנמאל דודי (Jeremiah 32:12), who was his uncle, and it is possible that he was older than Jeremiah in years, and he would call him by his father's name out of honor for the father. And so the wife of the father's brother Scripture called דודתך (Leviticus 18:14). But this 'the father of Canaan' is not so."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {0 "The phrase והוסיף תודות לשם is ambiguous; read as 'add praise to Shem' following the apparent argument. The final clause וזה אבי כנען איננו כן may also be rendered 'and this, \"my father Canaan,\" is not so,' depending on whether the missing word reconstructed is אבי or אבי."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:44:04.606427579Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}